WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.000
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and it's time to talk about the big reveals

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.180
in Solo: A Star Wars Story and what the film's
ending means for Star Wars, an Obi-Wan Kenobi

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.430
movie and possible Solo sequels.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:15.840
To celebrate the release of a new Star Wars
film, I'm running a Star Wars giveaway for

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.290
all my subscribers.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.880
For a chance to win, make sure you're subscribed
to my channel and leave a comment below with

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.450
your thoughts about the movie.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.720
Spoilers ahead for the Solo movie, so take
care if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.960
Let's start with the surprise reveal of Darth
Maul at the end of movie.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:34.761
If you last saw him get sliced in half by
Obi-Wan Kenobi in The Phantom Menace, you

00:00:34.761 --> 00:00:37.090
might be wondering how Maul is still alive.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:42.270
Well, the Sith Lord miraculously survived
Obi-Wan's blow and drop into the reactor shaft

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:46.610
using the Force to pull himself into an air
vent where he fell into a vat.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:50.540
Maul ended up being transported to another
planet where he was eventually rescued by

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.760
his brother.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.780
Fans of The Clone Wars and Rebels animated
TV series will have seen him in on the show

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.400
where he acquired robotic legs which you can
also see in the hologram of him in the Solo

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.400
movie.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.820
Maul is a popular prequel villain that some
fans have been hoping would return in a live-action

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.930
movie, and this brief appearance at the end
of Solo could be setting up the Sith Lord

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:15.120
as a series big bad who could span across
multiple Solo and other anthology and prequel

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.120
movies.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:21.170
And speaking to Maul was Qi'ra, who he commands
to come to him on Dathomir where they will

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:24.370
work together more closely, which means we'll
likely see Emilia Clarke returning in any

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.890
new movie with Darth Maul.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:30.030
By the way, notice in this scene that Darth
Maul wears the same kind of pendant we saw

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:36.229
Qi'ra wear when she saw Han in the Cantina
scene, it's a Crimson Dawn half-logo necklace.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:40.130
We get to see a darker side of Qi'ra in her
scene with Darth Maul where she seems to have

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.190
no trouble in lying to him claiming it was
Beckett who killed Dryden Vos when of course

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:45.240
she did.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.090
And there are numerous hints earlier in the
movie too about unspeakable things that Qi'ra's

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.090
done.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:53.020
As Beckett told Han at the end of the film,
'she's a survivor.'

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.530
Qi'ra's part in Solo ends with her piloting
Dryden's Space Yacht off to meet with Maul,

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:01.509
but as she leaves you can see she is a little
conflicted looking out at Han on the cliff

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:02.729
top below.

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:07.210
The filmmakers have said "Qi'ra is probably
the most complex character in the film" and

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.250
there are still things we need to learn about
her.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.829
For example, we don't know what Qi'ra had
to do to get off Corellia or what happened

00:02:12.829 --> 00:02:17.069
during the three years that she and Han were
separated or how she rose up the ranks of

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.989
the Crimson Dawn so quickly.

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:22.730
It's possible that's she's compromised in
some way to Darth Maul and maybe she thinks

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:25.889
she could put Han's life in danger if she
goes with him.

00:02:25.889 --> 00:02:29.709
Qi'ra does also seem resigned to her fate
saying to Han earlier in the movie that it's

00:02:29.709 --> 00:02:33.099
not about winning but how long you can stay
in the game.

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:36.930
And because she's a prequel character who
never appears or is mentioned in the original

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:41.569
trilogy, it's safe to say that Qi'ra probably
won't live beyond future sequels.

00:02:41.569 --> 00:02:45.700
By the way, there's a very cool musical easter
egg in the Maul and Qi'ra scene with some

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.349
of John Williams' "Duel of the Fates" playing
in the background.

00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:52.700
"Duel of the Fates" is a musical theme that
Williams composed for the prequel trilogy

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.910
and first played in The Phantom Menace during
the lightsaber battle between Darth Maul,

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.450
Qui-Gon and Obi-Wan.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:02.180
So, what could we see happen with Darth Maul
in a future movie?

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:06.370
Well, previously in The Clone Wars, Maul set
up a criminal organisation called the Shadow

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.370
Collective.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:11.579
In its heyday, the Collective totalled five
major criminal groups under its alliance,

00:03:11.579 --> 00:03:14.379
one of which was the Hutt Clan which had been
forced to join.

00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:18.260
The Hutts later abandoned the group and there
was a very big hint at the end of Solo that

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:22.260
the "big-shot gangster" they're heading off
to meet on Tatooine is Jabba the Hutt, meaning

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.590
that a sequel could have Han and Chewie forced
to go up against Maul, perhaps on behalf of

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:27.699
Jabba.

00:03:27.699 --> 00:03:31.449
Another member of Maul's Shadow Collective
was the Pyke Syndicate, and one of that gang's

00:03:31.449 --> 00:03:35.370
members also made a brief appearance in Solo
during the Kessel scenes.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:39.620
I also thought the placement of Mandalorian
armour in Dryden Vos's study is a nod to the

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:44.879
upcoming Boba Fett anthology movie that Logan
director James Mangold is working on for Lucasfilm.

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:49.450
Now, I do also think that there's an alternative
or additional movie that Darth Maul and perhaps

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:53.540
Qi'ra could appear in – which is the heavily
rumoured Obi-Wan Kenobi movie that a lot of

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.269
fans have been hoping for.

00:03:55.269 --> 00:03:59.640
Interestingly, Ewan McGregor appeared at the
Solo premiere even giving interviews.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:05.180
Obi-Wan struck the seemingly lethal blow to
Darth Maul in Episode 1, so the two have history,

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.620
but the potential wrinkle is that much of
this has been explored in the canon TV shows,

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:14.069
with the two even facing off for one fateful
final duel on Tatooine.

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:18.090
However, not everyone's familiar with the
animated series, so we could see a live-action

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.850
recreation of that duel in an Obi-Wan movie.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:24.490
The movie might also change some elements
of that story which has already been told

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.840
in the TV shows, although that might irk some
fans.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:33.440
But both Darth Maul and Obi-Wan are hugely
popular characters in the fandom and if Lucasfilm

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:37.120
sense there's an opportunity to capitalise
on that, I suspect they'll take it.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.120
A possible though maybe less likely option
is that Darth Maul's reappearance here is

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.120
to set up a major role for him in Jon Favreau's
new live-action TV series.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.040
I'm really pleased to see that Ray Park returned
as Darth Maul.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.680
Park played him in The Phantom Menace, and
in Solo, Maul's voice is provided by Sam Witwer

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.290
who's voiced the villain in the animated shows.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:51.770
Park seems like a really nice guy and when
I interviewed him before the new trilogy kicked

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.200
off, this is what he said about coming back
to Star Wars.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.010
"But deep down, I'd really like to come back
as Darth Maul."

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:58.010
"That's what I wanna do."

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.010
"I would do..

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:03.960
I would go crazy, go mental, lock myself in
a cabin, go.. you know."

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.180
"Do the whole method and.. for two or three
months.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.180
You know."

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:10.550
"Spear fishing and stuff and just to play
the character again."

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:14.840
As well as links to the prequels, Solo, of
course, connects to the original trilogy and

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:19.190
the reveal of Enfys Nest and her Cloud Rider
gang seems to be a nod to the early days of

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:20.220
the Rebel Alliance.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:25.200
And when Enfys Nest says to Han: "You could
come with us; we could use someone like you",

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:29.000
it's an interesting parallel with how Han
asked Luke to go with him and abandon the

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.670
Rebel Alliance, just before the attack on
the Death Star.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:33.060
"Why don't you come with us?"

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.040
"You're pretty good in a fight.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.580
We could use you."

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:37.580
"Come on.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.060
Why don't you take a look around?"

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.930
"You know what's about to happen, what they're
up against."

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:48.320
Now, Han doesn't go with Enfys Nest, preferring
instead to work on a big score for someone

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:53.620
like Jabba the Hutt, but like Qi'ra said to
Han "you're the good guy", and the Solo movie

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.960
is planting the seed for Han to eventually
do the right thing.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.080
Because Han did come back at the last minute
during the Death Star battle to save Luke.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:06.270
Later in Solo, Han tracks down Lando for a
final bet to win the Millennium Falcon.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:09.880
When he meets Lando, they hug just like they
do when they see each other in The Empire

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:10.880
Strikes Back.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.930
But Han, who knew that Lando was cheating
when he played him earlier in the Solo movie,

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:18.130
uses the hug to steal the card that Lando
had hidden up his sleeve.

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:22.940
Which is how Han eventually won the Millennium
Falcon and given that both Han and Lando cheated

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:27.140
in their Sabacc games, it brings an extra
level of meaning to this line from Empire:

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.900
"What have you done to my ship?"

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:29.900
"Your ship?"

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:33.610
"Hey, remember, you lost her to me fair and
square."

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:38.570
The other important moment at the end of Solo
is Han's final confrontation with Beckett.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:43.360
Over the course of the movie, we can detect
Beckett's cynical influence on Han.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:48.060
Beckett betrayed him to Dryden Vos, telling
Han earlier in the movie "assume everyone

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:52.280
will betray you and you'll never be disappointed",
and then, of course, Qi'ra did leave Han at

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.380
the end too.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:58.100
In his stand-off against Beckett, Han doesn't
hesitate to shoot first, demonstrating he's

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.750
internalised these sceptical views about honour
and betrayal and, of course, reminding us

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.560
of that scene with Greedo in A New Hope.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:09.510
So, what did you think of Solo and how does
it compare with your other favourite Star

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:10.860
Wars movies?

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:14.830
And do you have any predictions on how Darth
Maul, Qi'ra or Han and Chewie could return

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:15.990
in a sequel?

